.nh
.TH "CITADEL" "1" "Sep 2026" "AceTeam" "Citadel CLI Manual"

.SH NAME
citadel-status - Shows a comprehensive status of the Citadel node


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBcitadel status [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Provides a full health check and resource overview of the Citadel node.
It checks network connectivity, system vitals (CPU, RAM, Disk), GPU status,
and the state of all managed services.

.PP
The Backend: line reports whether this node's durable heartbeat write is
reaching the AceTeam control plane (reachable/degraded/DOWN/unknown). Note:
in direct-Redis mode this measures reachability of redis.aceteam.ai, not the
HTTPS API; in the normal API mode (post-'citadel init'), they are the same
backend.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for status

.PP
\fB-i\fP, \fB--interactive\fP[=false]
	Launch interactive dashboard with live updates

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Output in JSON format


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Enable debug output

.PP
\fB--no-auto-update\fP[=false]
	Disable automatic update checks and installs for this run (or set CITADEL_NO_AUTO_UPDATE=1)

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	Disable colorized output

.PP
\fB--node-dir\fP=""
	Override the node config directory (citadel.yaml + services/), bypassing $HOME/ConfigDir resolution. Also settable via CITADEL_NODE_DIR. Scope: manifest/services resolution only -- does NOT redirect network state, the module lockfile, or nodevault.

.PP
\fB--runtime\fP=""
	Container runtime for module containers: docker or podman (default: auto-detect)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  # View full node status with colors
  citadel status

  # View status without colors (for scripts/logging)
  citadel status --no-color

  # Interactive dashboard with live updates
  citadel status -i
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBcitadel(1)\fP
